  "problem": "| $z$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.5\\,$ | $\\,0.9345\\,$ | $\\,0.9357\\,$ | $\\,0.9370\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.6\\,$ | $\\,0.9463\\,$ | $\\,0.9474\\,$ | $\\,0.9484\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.7\\,$ | $\\,0.9564\\,$ | $\\,0.9573\\,$ | $\\,0.9582\\,$ |\n\nApproximate the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.9480$ using interval bisection and the above table.\n\n$z\u2248$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the two numbers in the table that $0.9480$ lies between. These numbers are $0.9474$ and $0.9484.$ So, we have the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.9474 & <0.9480<0.9484\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above inequality in terms of $\u03a6,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u03a6(1.62) & <\u03a6(z)<\u03a6(1.63).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using interval bisection, we can approximate $z$ as\n\n$$\nz\u2248\\frac{1.62+1.63}{2}=1.625.\n$$",
